
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
S5 · Prompts: server.registerPrompt + completable()
SDK: registerPrompt, completable, client.listPrompts, client.getPrompt, client.complete (ref/prompt)
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

▶ Prompts and their arguments
  listPrompts()
  ✔ 4ms → 
    [
      {
        "name": "class_report",
        "title": "Class performance report",
        "arguments": [
          {
            "name": "class_id",
            "description": "Class ID, e.g. \"IT01\"",
            "required": true
          },
          {
            "name": "semester",
            "description": "Semester, e.g. \"2024-1\"; empty = all semesters",
            "required": false
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "study_advice",
        "title": "Study advice for a student",
        "arguments": [
          {
            "name": "student_id",
            "description": "Student ID, e.g. \"2201005\"",
            "required": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ]

── getPrompt with parameter sets ─────────────────────────────────────────────

▶ class_report · required argument only
  getPrompt({"name":"class_report","arguments":{"class_id":"IT01"}})
  ✔ 3ms → 
    [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Write a performance report for class IT01 (all semesters).\nUse the tools class_statistics and rank_students (and calculate_gpa when needed). The report must include:\n1. Overview: number of students, average course total, pass rate, average GPA\n2. Letter-grade distribution (A/B/C/D/F)\n3. Top 3 students with GPA\n4. Students at risk (cumulative GPA below 2.0)\n5. Two concrete recommendations\nFormat it as Markdown. If a save_report tool is available, save the report as well."
      }
    ]

▶ class_report · with optional semester
  getPrompt({"name":"class_report","arguments":{"class_id":"BA02","semester":"2024-2"}})
  ✔ 2ms → 
    [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Write a performance report for class BA02 (semester 2024-2).\nUse the tools class_statistics and rank_students (and calculate_gpa when needed). The report must include:\n1. Overview: number of students, average course total, pass rate, average GPA\n2. Letter-grade distribution (A/B/C/D/F)\n3. Top 3 students with GPA\n4. Students at risk (cumulative GPA below 2.0)\n5. Two concrete recommendations\nFormat it as Markdown. If a save_report tool is available, save the report as well."
      }
    ]

▶ class_report · missing class_id → ProtocolError -32602
  getPrompt({"name":"class_report","arguments":{}})
  ✖ 2ms → ProtocolError (code -32602): Invalid arguments for prompt class_report: class_id: Invalid input: expected string, received undefined

▶ study_advice · embeds a resource in the message
  getPrompt({"name":"study_advice","arguments":{"student_id":"2201010"}})
  ✔ 2ms → 
    [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "type": "resource",
        "text": "[embedded academic://students/2201010]"
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "type": "text",
        "text": "You are an academic advisor. Using the profile above and the get_transcript tool, give this student 3 specific pieces of study advice: which courses to prioritise, whether any course should be retaken, and a realistic GPA target for next semester."
      }
    ]

▶ unknown prompt name
  getPrompt({"name":"does_not_exist","arguments":{}})
  ✖ 1ms → ProtocolError (code -32602): Prompt does_not_exist not found

── Argument autocompletion (completable) ─────────────────────────────────────

▶ class_report.class_id = ""
  complete({"ref":{"type":"ref/prompt","name":"class_report"},"argument":{"name":"class_id","value":""}})
  ✔ 2ms → 
    {
      "values": [
        "BA01",
        "BA02",
        "IT01",
        "IT02"
      ],
      "total": 4,
      "hasMore": false
    }

▶ class_report.class_id = "B"
  complete({"ref":{"type":"ref/prompt","name":"class_report"},"argument":{"name":"class_id","value":"B"}})
  ✔ 1ms → 
    {
      "values": [
        "BA01",
        "BA02"
      ],
      "total": 2,
      "hasMore": false
    }

▶ class_report.semester = "2024"
  complete({"ref":{"type":"ref/prompt","name":"class_report"},"argument":{"name":"semester","value":"2024"},"context":{"arguments":{"class_id":"IT01"}}})
  ✔ 1ms → 
    {
      "values": [],
      "hasMore": false
    }

